{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791031359,"nonce":"c8xCt/VxhUPHTEm+40f8Zz7B3IY=","title":"Android and iOS hosts: run a program with cb_window's event-loop hook","message":"Caribou has no host for Android or iOS: no android_main, and no iOS main that runs a program. cb_window now exports xwindow's hook (attach, Drive, winit) and the android-native-activity, android-game-activity and android-main features. What remains needs a host to put it in.\n\n- Android: android_main builds the loop with the AndroidApp, EventLoop::builder().with_android_app(app), and calls caribou_window::attach(events, Drive::Pump) before the program runs, or Drive::Turns with the program run in turns.\n- iOS: winit cannot pump, so main calls attach with Drive::Turns and never returns. A window opens only in a turn; poll and wait do not block, and the last empty one says when the next turn comes. The program has to run as turns, which the scheduler would drive.\n\nxwindow's CONTRIBUTING.md, \"The host's hook\", is the contract; xwindow-check's examples/host runs a program both ways on a desktop. cb_window builds for aarch64-linux-android (both activities, and with android-main) and aarch64-apple-ios.\n\nSplit from 1aec181, whose adapter part is done.","files":null}]}